  "notes": "SOURCE: Official Rowan University term-by-term sequence: 'Suggested Course Sequence -- BACHELOR OF SCIENCE IN COMPUTER SCIENCE' (csm.rowan.edu/departments/cs/advising/undergrad/bs_cs/BSsuggestedCourseSequence.pdf), revised 29 October 2019 -- this is the official term-by-term plan still posted by the Rowan CS department. Term placement, credits, and semester totals (15/15/16/16/16/16/15/12 = 121 sh) are transcribed exactly as printed. Course-number verification source: 'Accelerated Dual Degree Program Computer Science (O700/G700)' academic program guide, updated June 2026 (csm.rowan.edu/departments/cs/advising/program-guides/4+1s/cadp-bscs-to-mscs-program-guide---rowan-core.pdf), which contains the full current BS CS requirement list (64-65 sh program + 27 sh Rowan Core/Experience + 28 sh free electives = 120-121 sh total). RENUMBERING (1:1 verified against the June 2026 guide): CS 01205 -> CS 04215 Computer Lab Techniques; CS 07321 -> CS 04321 Software Engineering I; CS 04390 -> CS 06395 Operating Systems; CS 07351 -> CS 03351 Cyber Security: Fundamentals, Principles, & Applications; MATH 03160 -> MATH 03150 Discrete Mathematics; INTR 01266 -> INTR 01265 Computers and Society. Titles use current catalog wording. CREDIT CAVEAT: the printed sequence gives CS 04114 Object-Oriented Programming & Data Abstraction 2 sh (semester 2 totals 15 sh as printed); the June 2026 catalog lists that course at 3 sh. Credits are kept as printed so the plan sums to the sequence's own published total of 121 sh, which sits inside the catalog's published 120-121 sh degree total. CURRENT-CATALOG ADDITIONS NOT IN THE 2019 SEQUENCE (not placed in any term -- see advisor): WA 01302 Technical Writing (3 sh, Writing Intensive) became a required non-program course in Fall 2022 (it replaced the WI version of Computers and Society; the 2019 sequence carried WI on CS 07321 Software Engineering I); CS 06210 Advanced Computing Technologies (3 sh) was added to the foundational major list after 2019. TRANSCRIPTION: PDF downloaded via curl and text extracted with pdftotext; two-column semester layout manually reconciled against the department's own search-index rendering of the same document. Prereqs are asserted ONLY where verified from Rowan Banner catalog records (CS 04114 requires CS 04113; CS 04222 requires CS 04114 + MATH 03150 and CS 04215, which may be taken concurrently per Banner; CS 07210 requires CS 04113 + MATH 03150). CS 04113 has math-readiness placement (Calculus I readiness); not a course prereq. Free-elective slots total 27 sh across the sequence vs 28 sh in the current guide; use free electives to finish any remaining Rowan Core/Experience attributes per advisor. Rowan Core recommendation (June 2026): scientific literacy via BIOL 01104, CHEM 06100, or PHYS 00220; full authorized lab-science bank (ASTR/BIOL/CHEM/PHYS/BINF/MCB) is listed in the June 2026 guide. DS 02395 Topics in Data Science (1-3 sh) is also an eligible restricted elective per the guide but excluded from option lists because of its variable credit. catalog.rowan.edu content pages return bot-protection (http-202) responses, so all data above comes from the two official rowan.edu-hosted PDFs.",
